Compound feed denotes a scientifically formulated blend of cereals, protein meals, vitamins, minerals and additives designed to meet the nutritional requirements of livestock such as poultry, swine, cattle and aquaculture species.
The upward trend originates from growing consumer demand for animal derived protein as world populations expand, while advances in precision feeding technologies improve conversion ratios and reduce waste. Companies including Cargill, Archer Daniels Midland and Nutreco have broadened their portfolios through new additive lines and digital nutrition platforms introduced in early 2024.
